  ['singlefile', 'singlefile (Incremental) and wholemodule', 'The Swift Compilation Mode. Xcode shows singlefile as "Incremental": files compile separately, so an edit recompiles only what depends on it, which is right for Debug. "Whole Module" compiles the module as one job: faster code for Release, slower to iterate.'],
  ['housekeeping', 'Housekeeping', 'Findings with no impact band at all: neither measured on a build nor estimated by the rule catalog. Worth doing, but measure before and after; they come after the actions. How sure xcblame is shows on every finding and never moves it here.'],
  ['xcode-own-work', 'Xcode\'s own work', 'Rows such as "build system" and "explicit modules" are not targets of your project: Xcode planning the build and precompiling system modules (Foundation, AppKit…). You cannot shorten them by editing a target.'],
  ['changed-task', 'Changed task (compare)', 'A task that ran in both builds but with another key and command line (a new Xcode rewrites them). xcblame pairs it by rule, target and name and shows its seconds in both builds.'],
  ['swift-compile', 'swiftCompile', 'Compiling Swift source files into object files.'],
