  ['rule-id', 'Rule id', 'The short name of a rule, like SET-016: SET build settings, SRC Swift code, GRAPH project structure, PHASE build phases and scripts, DEP dependencies, ENV this Mac and Xcode, CI continuous integration, DYN measured on your build. `xcblame rules explain <id>` prints the whole rule.'],
  ['validation', 'Checks V1-V15', 'Self-checks xcblame runs on its own numbers, for example "the target rows add up to the total". A failed check withholds the number it protects.'],
  ['data-quality', 'Data quality (degraded)', 'Shown when the input missed something (a log section, the build description), so some numbers are unknown or less precise. The note next to each such number says what.'],
  ['redacted', 'Redacted', 'User names, home paths and host names are replaced (with ~ and $USER) so the file is safe to share.'],
  ['truncation', 'Shortened list', 'A long list cut to keep this file under its size cap. Totals still count every row; the line under the list gives the command that prints every row.'],
  ['clean-build', 'Clean build', 'A build from nothing: every task runs.'],
